<p>Calculate the density of aluminum if 27.6 cm<sup>3</sup> has a mass of 74.6 g.</p>






 

<div class="ui-toggle-wrapper"> </div>





<section class="ui-body">
<p>2.70 g/cm<sup>3</sup></p>
</section>






<p>Osmium is one of the densest elements known. What is its density if 2.72 g has a volume of 0.121 cm<sup>3</sup>?</p>







<p>Calculate these masses.</p>

<p>(a) What is the mass of 6.00 cm<sup>3</sup> of mercury, density = 13.5939 g/cm<sup>3</sup>?</p>

<p>(b) What is the mass of 25.0 mL octane, density = 0.702 g/cm<sup>3</sup>?</p>


<div class="ui-toggle-wrapper"> </div>





<div class="ui-toggle-wrapper"> </div>

<section class="ui-body">
<p>(a) 81.6 g; (b) 17.6 g</p>
</section>






<p>Calculate these masses.</p>

<ol>
    <li>(a) What is the mass of 4.00 cm<sup>3</sup> of sodium, density = 0.97 g/cm?</li>
    <li>(b) What is the mass of 125 mL gaseous chlorine, density = 3.16 g/L?</li>
</ol>







<p>Calculate these volumes.</p>

<ol>
    <li>(a) What is the volume of 25 g iodine, density = 4.93 g/cm<sup>3</sup>?</li>
    <li>(b) What is the volume of 3.28 g gaseous hydrogen, density = 0.089 g/L?</li>
</ol>






<div class="ui-toggle-wrapper"> </div>

<section class="ui-body">
<p>(a) 5.1 mL; (b) 37 L</p>
</section>






<p>Calculate these volumes.</p>

<ol>
    <li>(a) What is the volume of 11.3 g graphite, density = 2.25 g/cm<sup>3</sup>?</li>
    <li>(b) What is the volume of 39.657 g bromine, density = 2.928 g/cm<sup>3</sup>?</li>
</ol>







